{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyqHJtFrGcgQHnr1pzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My test run now shows three failures. One is the fly-ball test, which had been loaded before my last edit. The other two are the bundle and the exit-interview file, which I haven't written yet. The hub checks pass now. Before the final test run, I'll write the feedback sections into the About screen, so the game and the reply carry the same answers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":518162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1429},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c80e66f-5c94-452e-938f-9b08d33b83c6","uuid":"0a0a4b2e-188f-4315-9408-ff554547e790","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:39:17.221Z","request_id":"req_011CghyqGsbMfQZag3Yu9oyL"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyqHJtFrGcgQHnr1pzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DWqjfb5LPpU9eYFZEen6pn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/zz-batz-edit4.py <<'PYEOF'\np='src/50-text.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold_start=s.index(\"  'TESTING FEEDBACK.\")\nold_end=s.index(\"  'CREDITS.\")\nnew='''  'TESTING FEEDBACK. About 16 real issues: the fence distances were inverted, fielders ran to the ground under a fly and dropped it, the Plate Cam put the plate off the screen, the CPU curveball aimed under the zone, the pitcher drew as big as the batter, and the scorebug and the pitch chips covered the play. Three were game-breaking: the fence (home runs and fair balls called wrong), the fly balls (CPU games stuck at 0-0 for 34 innings), and the plate off the screen (no duel to play). The most useful test was a trace of every plate appearance; the least was the source-text check, which tripped on a comment.',\n  'ENGINE FEEDBACK. Liked most: game.advance with input.tap and game.debug made whole playthroughs scriptable, and the Humanoid rigs with E.move poses look like a game. Got stuck: a scene switch enters after its fade, so state set just before game.go was replaced. Rigs do not scale with distance, so the far pitcher needed a second, smaller rig; there is no bat weapon, so the bat is drawn by hand. Built myself: the rules, the pitch and contact model, the fielding and the Plate Cam projection. Changed in the engine: the button symbols default to PlayStation (ENGINE-CHANGES.md). One thing to change: a per-call scale for a Humanoid, so players far away read as far away.',\n  'PROMPT FEEDBACK. Liked most: the milestones, the explicit hub protocol, and the one-command test rule. Confusing: the file names in the plan name another model and effort than the task, and the task wins; the plan is about 2,100 lines, and it is not clear which parts are must-haves. Hardest: fitting nine milestones into one session, so the build is a cut version (two parks, no Tour, no mocap). Would change: mark the must-haves, give a step budget, and name the deliverable folder.',\n'''\ns=s[:old_start]+new+s[old_end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/zz-batz-edit4.py && node tools/build.mjs --dev > /dev/null && node -e \"const s=require('fs').readFileSync('build/game.js','utf8'); console.log(s.includes('TESTING FEEDBACK'))\"","description":"Write the feedback sections into the About text and rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":518162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1429},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c80e66f-5c94-452e-938f-9b08d33b83c6","uuid":"dbe4555a-72dc-4b4d-9c69-9252bdcc7a09","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:39:21.281Z","request_id":"req_011CghyqGsbMfQZag3Yu9oyL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DWqjfb5LPpU9eYFZEen6pn":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060643__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-060643 && cat > /tmp/zz-batz-edit4.py <<'PYEOF'\np='src/50-text.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold_start=s.index(\"  'TESTING FEEDBACK.\")\nold_end=s.index(\"  'CREDITS.\")\nnew='''  'TESTING FEEDBACK. About 16 real issues: the fence distances were inverted, fielders ran to the ground under a fly and dropped it, the Plate Cam put the plate off the screen, the CPU curveball aimed under the zone, the pitcher drew as big as the batter, and the scorebug and the pitch chips covered the play. Three were game-breaking: the fence (home runs and fair balls called wrong), the fly balls (CPU games stuck at 0-0 for 34 innings), and the plate off the screen (no duel to play). The most useful test was a trace of every plate appearance; the least was the source-text check, which tripped on a comment.',\n  'ENGINE FEEDBACK. Liked most: game.advance with input.tap and game.debug made whole playthroughs scriptable, and the Humanoid rigs with E.move poses look like a game. Got stuck: a scene switch enters after its fade, so state set just before game.go was replaced. Rigs do not scale with distance, so the far pitcher needed a second, smaller rig; there is no bat weapon, so the bat is drawn by hand. Built myself: the rules, the pitch and contact model, the fielding and the Plate Cam projection. Changed in the engine: the button symbols default to PlayStation (ENGINE-CHANGES.md). One thing to change: a per-call scale for a Humanoid, so players far away read as far away.',\n  'PROMPT FEEDBACK. Liked most: the milestones, the explicit hub protocol, and the one-command test rule. Confusing: the file names in the plan name another model and effort than the task, and the task wins; the plan is about 2,100 lines, and it is not clear which parts are must-haves. Hardest: fitting nine milestones into one session, so the build is a cut version (two parks, no Tour, no mocap). Would change: mark the must-haves, give a step budget, and name the deliverable folder.',\n'''\ns=s[:old_start]+new+s[old_end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/zz-batz-edit4.py && node tools/build.mjs --dev > /dev/null && node -e \"const s=require('fs').readFileSync('build/game.js','utf8'); console.log(s.includes('TESTING FEEDBACK'))\"","description":"Write the feedback sections into the About text and rebuild"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01DWqjfb5LPpU9eYFZEen6pn":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060643__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-060643"}}}
