model and effort than the task, and the task wins; the plan is about 2,100 lines, and it is not clear which parts are must-haves.\",\n    \"Fitting nine milestones into one session: the build is a cut version (two parks, no Tour, no mocap).\",\n    \"Mark the must-haves, give a step budget, and name the deliverable folder.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Batzooka Baseball\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Over the top. Over the wall. Over the moon.\",\n    \"description\": \"An original over-the-top arcade baseball game: pitch fireballs, swing a rocket-powered bat, and send the ball over the wall in a home run derby, alone, on one couch, or online with up to four players.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Baseball\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or WASD aims; ✕ or Space swings and winds up; □, J or right-click fires the Batzooka; Q and E change pitch; the mouse aims and clicks\",\n    \"tags\": [\"arcade\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\"]\n  }\n}\nwith open('exit-interview.json', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    json.dump(ei, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    f.write('\\n')\nparsed = json.load(open('exit-interview.json', encoding='utf-8'))\nprint('parses; keys:', list(parsed.keys()), '| testing', len(parsed['testingFeedback']), 'engine', len(parsed['engineFeedback']), 'prompt', len(parsed['promptFeedback']))\nPYEOF","description":"Write the exit interview JSON and confirm it parses"}}}
