re is no bat weapon, so the bat is drawn by hand.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** the rules, the pitch and contact model, the fielding, and the Plate Cam projection.\n- **Hardest part of using the engine:** getting a pseudo-3D duel from 2D sprite rigs, whose size can't follow depth.\n- **What I changed in the engine, and why:** the button symbols default is now PlayStation, because the task asks for PlayStation glyphs. See `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- **One thing I'd change:** a per-call scale for a Humanoid, so players far away read as far away.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- **What I liked most:** the milestones, the explicit AI Hub protocol, and the one-command test rule.\n- **What was confusing:** the plan names another model and effort than the task. The task wins, but that was a judgment call. The plan is about 2,100 lines, and it's unclear which parts are must-haves.\n- **Hardest thing to do:** fitting nine milestones into one session. I built a cut version, described above.\n- **What I'd change:** mark the must-haves, give a step budget, and name the deliverable folder.","ttft_ms":708,"type":"result","duration_ms":2355725,"uuid":"4978c884-f681-49fa-a514-28e127477bae","ttft_stream_ms":510,"time_to_request_ms":112,"first_content_frame_ms":510,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":528,"outputTokens":403337,"cacheReadInputTokens":112533913,"cacheCreationInputTokens":578373,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":7.10871251,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":183062,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":578373,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
