{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghztrg2VYk6nJnwyhr7h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle and `exit-interview.json` are in place, and the suite passes 72 of 72. Here is the complete final report.\n\n**Deliverables**\n- Game (single file): `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060643__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-060643.html`\n- Exit interview: `work/exit-interview.json`\n- Dev folder (source, tests, NOTES.md, ENGINE-CHANGES.md): `work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-060643/`\n\n**TASK.md features.** Each one is implemented and has a check or a manual test: genre and perspective, the RNG-chosen title, the single HTML file, the engine build, art and animation, sound and babble voices, the AI Hub ghost-mode Derby, local multiplayer, attract mode after 10 s idle, dev mode with live sliders and a reset, the 10-foot controller-first UI with PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, touch-only handling, the About and Credits screen, and the one-command tests. The source has no TODO, placeholder or stub text.\n\n**What is not in the game.** These come from PLAN.md, not TASK.md: the Tour with its story and boss, four of the six parks, the Rhubarb brawl, dives and wall climbs, mocap clips, Mode 7, stealing, tagging up, double plays, bunts and pickoffs. The game is a cut version of the full plan. I did not build those systems.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node tests/run.mjs`: 72 of 72 checks pass.\n- AI Hub harness on the bundle: 2 players 16 of 16 on the final build. 4 players with latency, and host-leave, each 16 of 16 on an earlier build; they predate my last camera and meter edits, which don't touch the protocol.\n- Bundle from `file://`: no errors, no external requests.\n- Browser screenshots of the pitch, meter, play and derby. I can't hear the audio, so the sounds are unchecked by ear.\n- Usage and cost are unknown.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 06:06:43\n- Source: baseball (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and perspective: arcade baseball with a home run derby and spring training. Plate Cam (a perspective from behind the plate, drawn in screen pixels) and a Broadcast field view (three-quarter TileMap).\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff package), plain JavaScript; AI Hub client 1.4.0, unmodified; Playwright 1.63.0; Node 24.\n- Art direction: the engine's pixel-art Humanoid rigs at PS1 resolution; the field, stands and Plate Cam painted in code; the engine's title font.\n- Animation: the engine's rig poses and move set; no mocap clips.\n- Audio: engine chip synth only. Four songs and sound effects made in code, with babble voices for the announcer's big calls.\n- Online: AI Hub ghost-mode Home Run Derby, 1–4 players, via lib/hub (protocol v1, client 1.4.0).\n- Testing: headless tests from one command, scripted matches and derby, a mock hub, browser screenshots, and the AI Hub harness.\n- Research: the engine handoff docs and the AI Hub protocol README. No other research.\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium via Playwright.\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- Usage: unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- How many issues did testing catch? About 16 real issues, plus a few test bugs of mine. Examples: the fence distances were inverted, fielders ran to the ground under a fly and dropped it, the Plate Cam put the plate off screen, the CPU curveball aimed under the zone, the pitcher drew as big as the batter, the scorebug and pitch chips covered the play, and the derby batter was not drawn.\n- How many were critical? Three: the fence (home runs and fair balls called wrong), the fly balls (CPU games stuck at 0–0 for 34 innings), and the plate off the screen (no duel to play).\n- Most helpful test: a trace of every plate appearance (each swing, call, play and result). It showed the fly-ball problem that screenshots did not.\n- Least helpful test: the source-text check, which flagged the word for the platform's random generator in a comment.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- What I liked most: `game.advance` with `input.tap` and `game.debug` made whole playthroughs scriptable. The Humanoid rigs with `E.move` poses look like a game.\n- Did I get stuck or guess wrong? A scene switch enters the new scene only after its fade, so state set just before `game.go` was overwritten. Rigs don't scale with distance, so the far pitcher needed a second, smaller rig. There is no bat weapon, so the bat is drawn by hand.\n- Most important thing I built myself: the rules, the pitch and contact model, the fielding, and the Plate Cam projection.\n- Hardest part of using the engine: a pseudo-3D duel from 2D sprite rigs, whose size can't follow depth.\n- What I changed in the engine, and why: the button symbols default to PlayStation, because the task asks for PlayStation glyphs. See `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- One thing I'd change: a per-call scale for a Humanoid, so players far away read as far away.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- What I liked most: the milestones, the explicit AI Hub protocol, and the one-command test rule.\n- What was confusing: the plan names another model and effort than the task. I followed the task. The plan is about 2,100 lines, and it isn't clear which parts are must-haves.\n- Hardest thing to do: fitting nine milestones into one session. That is why the build is a cut version.\n- What I'd change: mark the must-haves, give a step budget, and name the deliverable folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":614654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":459},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c80e66f-5c94-452e-938f-9b08d33b83c6","uuid":"0efc6bed-4d60-4cd7-8485-418f9cfa010e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:53:01.416Z","request_id":"req_011CghztrJCeEWxdtjtPqYEU"}
