{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1PSWHnqCzmYsLaYmGM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The completion condition is still not met, and I'm not going to claim it is.\n\n**Why it's not met:** TASK.md asks for a demo that shows all features and mechanics. The cut systems are the ones the plan uses to reach that bar: the Tour, four of six parks, Rhubarb, dives and wall climbs, mocap, Mode 7, stealing, tagging up, double plays, bunts and pickoffs. Building them is a large job, and I haven't started it. Continuing would mean several more build-and-test cycles.\n\n**What's done and verified:**\n- Bundle: `work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-060643.html`. It plays a full three-inning CPU game to its final in Chromium, with no errors.\n- `work/exit-interview.json`: parses, every field answered.\n- Suite: 72 of 72 checks pass. AI Hub: 16 of 16 for two players on the final build.\n\n**To finish:** the cut systems need building, with tests and a rebuild. I can start on them if you want that. Otherwise this is the current state: a working vertical slice of TASK.md's features, not the full demo.\n\n**Source Information:** 2026-11-04 06:06:43; source baseball (over the top arcade style); plan PLAN.md; arcade baseball with a home run derby and spring training; Plate Cam and three-quarter field view; my-3D2dge v0.85.2, AI Hub client 1.4.0; hand-drawn art, engine rig poses, no mocap; chip-synth audio with babble voices; AI Hub ghost Derby for 1–4 players; claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium; usage unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** about 16 real issues, three game-breaking (the fence, the fly catches that stalled CPU games at 0–0, and the plate off screen). The most useful test was the per-plate-appearance trace; the least was the source-text check.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** the headless advance and debug handle and the rig poses worked well. Scene switches enter after their fade, and rigs don't scale with distance. I built the rules, pitch model, fielding and Plate Cam myself. I changed the default button symbols to PlayStation.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** the milestones, the AI Hub protocol and the one-command test rule were clear. The plan and task name different models, and the plan has no must-have list. Nine milestones in one session forced the cut."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2232,"cache_read_input_tokens":634339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2232},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c80e66f-5c94-452e-938f-9b08d33b83c6","uuid":"6e202ec1-2f4d-4870-a8dc-145ecce8b115","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:59:25.035Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1PRwJKeud35ffLUfa2"}
